### Example 2: Cleaning Messy Excel Data

**The Situation:**
You receive a customer database with 500 rows. Names have inconsistent capitalization, emails have random spaces, and there are duplicate entries throughout.

**Traditional Method:** 
Manually review and fix each cell, use Find & Replace multiple times, visually scan for duplicates. Time: 30-45 minutes.

**Python Method:**
```python
import pandas as pd

# Open your messy Excel file
data = pd.read_excel("customer_database_messy.xlsx")

# Clean the Name column
data['Name'] = data['Name'].str.strip()  # Remove extra spaces
data['Name'] = data['Name'].str.title()  # Standardize Capitalization

# Clean the Email column
data['Email'] = data['Email'].str.lower()  # Make all lowercase
data['Email'] = data['Email'].str.strip()  # Remove spaces

# Clean the Phone column
data['Phone'] = data['Phone'].str.replace(" ", "")  # Remove spaces
data['Phone'] = data['Phone'].str.replace("-", "")  # Remove dashes

# Remove duplicate rows
data = data.drop_duplicates()

# Save the cleaned version
data.to_excel("customer_database_clean.xlsx", index=False)

print(f"Cleaned! Removed {data.duplicated().sum()} duplicates.")
```

**What this does:**
- Opens your Excel file
- Removes extra spaces from text
- Standardizes formatting (capitalization, phone formats)
- Identifies and removes duplicate entries
- Saves a clean version

**Time saved:** 30+ minutes per file

